{"id":"windows/settings/customize","platform":"windows","kind":"csp","surface":"settings","identifier":"customize","name":"Customize","description":"Windows MDM settings in the Customize category, applied as OMA-URI (SyncML) values.","group":"Microsoft Office 2016","properties":[{"key":"L_AllowRoamingQuickAccessToolBarRibbonCustomizations","name":"Allow roaming of all user customizations (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows roaming of both the Quick Access Toolbar and Ribbon customizations. \n\nIf you enable this policy setting, users' Quick Access Toolbar and Ribbon customizations will be available to them on any computer on their network when they log on. \n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, users' Quick Access Toolbar and Ribbon customizations will only be available to them on the computer on which they made the customizations.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_GloablOptions~L_Customize/L_AllowRoamingQuickAccessToolBarRibbonCustomizations","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v2"},{"key":"L_DefaultUIThemeMachine","name":"Default Office theme","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows you to select the user interface (UI) theme used by Office, if the user has not already selected an Office theme.\n\nNote: This setting only applies to Version 1903 or later of Office.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, you may choose the Office theme used in cases where the user has not selected an Office theme themselves.\n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Office will use the Colorful theme in cases where the user has not selected an Office theme themselves.\n\nRegardless of how you configure this policy setting, users can change their Office theme by going to File > Account > Office Theme (or, in Outlook, by going to File > Office Account > Office Theme).\n\nNote: This policy setting takes precedence over the “Default Office theme” policy setting located under User Configuration.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v3~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficemachine~L_GlobalOptionsMachine~L_CustomizeMachine/L_DefaultUIThemeMachine","scope":"device","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v3"},{"key":"L_DefaultUIThemeUser","name":"Default Office theme (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows you to select the user interface (UI) theme used by Office, if the user has not already selected an Office theme.\n\nNote: This setting only applies to Version 1903 or later of Office.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, you may choose the Office theme used in cases where the user has not selected an Office theme themselves.\n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Office will use the Colorful theme in cases where the user has not selected an Office theme themselves.\n\nRegardless of how you configure this policy setting, users can change their Office theme by going to File > Account > Office Theme (or, in Outlook, by going to File > Office Account > Office Theme).\n\nNote: The “Default Office theme” policy setting located under Computer Configuration takes precedence over this policy setting.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v3~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_GlobalOptions~L_Customize/L_DefaultUIThemeUser","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v3"},{"key":"L_NoExtensibilityCustomizationFromDocumentPolicy","name":"Disable UI extending from documents and templates (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting controls whether Office 2016 applications load any custom user interface (UI) code included with a document or template. Office 2016 allows developers to extend the UI with customization code that is included in a document or template. \n\nIf you enable this policy setting, Office 2016 applications cannot load any UI customization code included with documents and templates. \n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Office 2016 applications load any UI customization code included with a document or template when opening it.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_GloablOptions~L_Customize/L_NoExtensibilityCustomizationFromDocumentPolicy","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v2"},{"key":"L_NoExtensibilityCustomizationFromDocumentPolicyAccess","name":"Disallow in Access (User)","type":"enum","description":"","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"False"},{"value":"1","description":"True"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_GloablOptions~L_Customize/L_NoExtensibilityCustomizationFromDocumentPolicy","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v2"},{"key":"L_NoUserCustomizationPolicyAccess","name":"Disallow in Access (User)","type":"enum","description":"","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"False"},{"value":"1","description":"True"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_GloablOptions~L_Customize/L_NoUserCustomizationPolicy","scope":"user","introducedI